---
title: When to Use a Class (Two-of-Five Rule)
---
flowchart TD
    Q([Should I create a class?])
    Q --> C1{State + behaviour<br/>always travel together?}
    Q --> C2{Multiple independent<br/>instances expected?}
    Q --> C3{State must persist<br/>across many operations?}
    Q --> C4{Clear creation/<br/>mutation/disposal lifecycle?}
    Q --> C5{Polymorphism / multiple<br/>types share interface?}

    C1 --> COUNT[Count 'Yes' answers]
    C2 --> COUNT
    C3 --> COUNT
    C4 --> COUNT
    C5 --> COUNT

    COUNT --> D{Two or more 'Yes'?}
    D -->|Yes| USE["✅ Use a class<br/>(or @dataclass)"]
    D -->|No| FN["⚠️ Use a function<br/>or a dataclass without methods"]

    classDef question fill:#3776ab,stroke:#1e4870,color:#ffffff,stroke-width:2px
    classDef criterion fill:#fff3cd,stroke:#f59e0b,color:#1a1410
    classDef decision fill:#e8f0f8,stroke:#3776ab,color:#0b1020
    classDef good fill:#d1fae5,stroke:#10b981,color:#064e3b
    classDef warn fill:#fee2e2,stroke:#ef4444,color:#7f1d1d
    class Q question
    class C1,C2,C3,C4,C5 criterion
    class COUNT,D decision
    class USE good
    class FN warn
